  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The unit of intelligence is no longer the model",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "1. The Loop Is the Product",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Traditional AI systems are static:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Autoresearch systems are dynamic:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The key idea is that the feedback loop itself becomes the product surface",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "But the hard problem isn't building loops—it's designing signals that are meaningful enough for improvement without collapsing into noisy optimization",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Expensive signals (expert review, structured evals) are what actually move capability",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "A core concept is the agent recipe",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "An agent recipe is not configuration—it is history:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The outer loop is where improvement happens",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The inner loop is where value is delivered",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The key design challenge is ensuring the outer loop remains cost-bounded and signal-efficient, not a runaway optimization engine",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Humans are not outside the system. They are callable components inside the loop, especially early on",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "These are not reasoning-heavy tasks. They are judgment-heavy tasks",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Prompts can only encode what experts can articulate. The most important judgments are often non-verbalizable",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not incremental improvement. It is a regime shift in how capability is produced",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "On-policy distillation: prevents degradation over time",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
